{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalFourierTransformExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalFourierTransformExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QIntegralTransforms"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalFourier.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalFourier.exists","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-exists.lean#L27-L49","doc":"**Existence of the categorical Fourier transform.**\n\nFor any categorical Laplace transform `L` on `A` and any family of\nspectral parameters `s : Irreps → R_q`, there exists a\n`CategoricalFourier A Irreps` whose projections are the Wick-rotated\nLaplace transforms `project_j f = L.transform f (s j)`.\n\nThis replaces the earlier `Nonempty (CategoricalFourier A Irreps)` proved\nby the input-ignoring witness `project := fun _ _ => id` (whose monoidal\nlaw held vacuously because both sides collapsed to `id`): the existential\nnow pins the projections to the genuine Wick rotation of `L`, and the\nFourier monoidal law is *derived* from `L.monoidal_mul` rather than holding\nvacuously — realising [`def:categorical-fourier`]'s\n`F[f](ξ) = L[f](iξ)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-fourier-exists","label":"prop:categorical-fourier-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-exists.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0}]}